WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.750
IRIV EdgeAI CM5
An industrial AI controller that sees, thinks and acts.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.250
Sees. Thinks. Acts.
Sees: 2× MIPI CSI, Industrial cameras, IP and CCTV cameras. Thinks: Up to 26 TOPS, Raspberry Pi CM5, Up to 16 GB. Acts: 2 dry contacts, 2 drivers, 2 A each, RS485 and 2× Gigabit.

3
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:18.250
Check every bottle.
A sensor triggers the camera, the AI checks each bottle, and faulty ones are rejected.

4
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.750
Everything wires in at the front.
16 push-in terminals, two Gigabit ports, status LEDs and Wi-Fi.

5
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.950
10–30 V DC in.
Surge protected up to 60 V for 20 ms, and 11 W at full load, so a standard 24 V DIN-rail supply runs it with room for lights and sensors.

6
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.150
Isolated RS485.
Up to 500 kbps with 5000 Vrms isolation. Send results to a PLC over Modbus, or read meters and sensors next to the camera.

7
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.750
Two trigger inputs.
Isolated and bidirectional, 3–50 V high. Wire a photoelectric sensor to DI0 so a part arriving triggers the camera. S/S is the shared common for sinking or sourcing sensors.

8
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.250
Two dry-contact outputs.
Isolated relay-style contacts, up to 50 V and 500 mA. Fire a reject pusher, open a barrier or switch a stack light when the AI decides.

9
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.850
Built-in light drivers.
L0 and L1 power inspection lights straight from VIN, up to 2 A each, with PWM dimming. Strobe a ring or dome light in time with each capture.

10
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.350
Two Gigabit ports.
Bring in IP and CCTV cameras over RTSP on one port, and send results to the plant or cloud on the other.

11
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.150
Status at a glance.
Power, activity, M.2, 4G power and WWAN LEDs, two programmable LEDs, a programmable USER button and a POWER button. An OLED and a buzzer are inside.

12
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.950
USB-C for setup.
Flash the eMMC and debug over USB-C. Day to day you log in over the network.

13
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.150
Wireless, built in.
Dual-band 2.4 / 5 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth 5.0 with BLE. The antenna is included.

14
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.150
Two MIPI camera ports.
Two 4-lane MIPI CSI ports take Raspberry Pi cameras directly, with no USB bandwidth used. Run two cameras on one controller, such as top and side views of the same part.

15
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.950
USB 3.0 and 4K HDMI.
Two USB 3.0 ports carry high-resolution industrial cameras at full speed. HDMI 2.0 drives a 4K 60 Hz screen for live inspection results.

16
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.450
4G, anywhere.
An mPCIe socket (USB 2.0) takes a 4G or LoRa module, with the SIM slot on the side. The 4G PWR and WWAN LEDs on the front show its status.

17
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.950
Read every plate.
The IP camera tracks cars and people, reads each plate and opens the barrier.

18
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.450
Up to 26 TOPS of AI.
13 TOPS: Raspberry Pi AI HAT+, 13 TOPS, Raspberry Pi CM5, Cortex-A76 2.4 GHz, 8 GB LPDDR4-4267, 32 GB. 26 TOPS: Raspberry Pi AI HAT+, 26 TOPS, Raspberry Pi CM5, Cortex-A76 2.4 GHz, 8 or 16 GB LPDDR4-4267, 32 or 64 GB.

19
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.650
Clips onto a DIN rail.
A metal, fanless case, 139 × 88 × 38 mm, rated −20 to 60 °C. It clips onto a standard 35 mm rail next to the camera’s power supply.

20
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.650
IRIV EdgeAI CM5
Defect detection · OCR · counting · ANPR · CCTV analytics. From RM2,487 at cytron.io.

